        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: add ClawHub glossary labels",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nGenerated zh-CN documentation does not have exact glossary mappings for the existing `ClawHub CLI` and `Publishing on ClawHub` labels. When the docs i18n pipeline sees those labels, it needs stable source terms so localized navigation and page-title output do not drift.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe branch preserves the existing ClawHub mirrored navigation contract and only adds glossary labels for the existing `ClawHub CLI` and `Publishing on ClawHub` titles. It does not add local OpenClaw-owned ClawHub pages or remove any mirror-owned ClawHub routes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nReaders of localized docs get consistent ClawHub labels while the published ClawHub docs navigation continues to expose the routes supplied by the ClawHub mirror.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Branch rebased and pushed on `origin/main` `1185db56c0d55b5bb05e4af8756368558adbf63f`; pushed head is `dc91a741a9c7b4097a2eccadfcff06a940dc162f`.\n- Post-rebase diff against that base: `docs/.i18n/glossary.zh-CN.json` only, 8 insertions.\n- Confirmed the branch only adds exact zh-CN glossary entries for `ClawHub CLI` and `Publishing on ClawHub`.\n- GitHub Codex review thread for the original missing-glossary feedback is already resolved and outdated.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` - passed.\n- `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('docs/.i18n/glossary.zh-CN.json','utf8')); console.log('json ok')\"` - passed.\n- `pnpm docs:check-i18n-glossary` - passed. Local run warned that Node `v24.14.1` is below the repo's Node engine floor for this checkout; the command exited `0`.",
